# pherolang.com — response headers for the Cloudflare Worker's static assets.
#
# Cloudflare Workers reads this file from the directory it serves
# (`dist/client`, per `wrangler.jsonc`) and applies the rules to asset
# responses, in file order. Three properties of that format shape everything
# below:
#
#   * a request matching several rules inherits the headers of EVERY matching
#     rule, and a header set twice is joined with a comma — so `Cache-Control`
#     must be set exactly once per response, which is why the `/_astro/*` rule
#     detaches the broader value before setting its own;
#   * `! Name` removes only what EARLIER rules added, so the narrower rule has
#     to come after the broader one;
#   * `_headers` applies to asset responses only. Both apps deploy as
#     assets-only Workers (`wrangler deploy --dry-run` reports "No bindings
#     found"), so every response a visitor sees passes through this file.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is derived from the built HTML, not from theory.
# `site/DEPLOY.md` records which directive is relaxed, the evidence for it, and
# what to change before adding a script or an analytics beacon.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Hashed build output (`index.<hash>.css`, `<island>.<hash>.js`): the filename
# changes when the bytes change, so it can be cached forever. The detach keeps
# the `/*` rule from joining a second, contradictory max-age onto the value.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Version-preview and workers.dev hostnames are not canonical. The apex and
# `www` hostnames are; anything served from `*.workers.dev` is a duplicate of a
# page that already has a canonical URL, so keep it out of the index. Preview
# URLs look like `<version>-<worker>.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev`, which is
# the placeholder shape Cloudflare documents for this file (one splat per rule
# is the limit, and a hostname wildcard plus a path wildcard is two).
https://:version.:subdomain.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
